# Files in the repo root that must NOT be uploaded as public static assets.
#
# The repo root IS the asset directory (see wrangler.toml [assets]), so without
# this file every path below would be fetchable on joinshug.com. Server code and
# schema being publicly readable is not a secret leak — there are no secrets in
# them — but it is needless attack surface and it wastes the asset budget.
#
# Syntax is .gitignore syntax. _headers, _redirects and this file are consumed
# as configuration by the runtime and are never served, so they need no entry.

# Server-side code. Runs in the worker; must never be served as a file.
worker/
functions/

# Schema, migrations, seeds, tests, maintenance scripts.
migrations/
tests/
tools/
*.sql

# Repo documentation and configuration.
*.md
wrangler.toml
package.json
.editorconfig

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS. A dry run WITHOUT these lines served /.dev.vars with a 200 and the
# real Retell API key in the body. .dev.vars is gitignored, which protects it
# from the repository and does nothing whatsoever about the asset bundle — the
# asset directory is the working tree, not the git index.
#
# Both the bare name and the glob are listed: .gitignore syntax does not treat
# `.dev.vars` as also matching `.dev.vars.local`, and a variant file appearing
# later must not silently become public.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.env
.env.*

# The git directory. Wrangler does NOT exclude this on its own — a dry-run
# without this line reported 935 asset files against a 28-page site, because it
# was about to publish the entire repository history. Anything ever committed
# would have been fetchable at https://joinshug.com/.git/... . Do not remove.
.git/

# Local state that should never reach a deploy in the first place.
.wrangler/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
